+- **Node's `fetch` ignores `HTTPS_PROXY`; `curl` does not.** The same GitHub API
+  request returns 200 under `curl` and `401 Bad credentials` under node's global
+  `fetch`, because the proxy is what supplies working credentials and node goes
+  direct. Run with `NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1` (node 22+). Read as "my token is
+  wrong", this costs an hour chasing the wrong thing — the token is fine.
+- **`GITHUB_TOKEN` and `GH_TOKEN` can both be set with only one valid.** Measured
+  2026-08-23: `GITHUB_TOKEN` 401s, `GH_TOKEN` works. Prefer `GH_TOKEN` first,
+  which is `gh`'s own precedence and the order that works in both environments.
+- **A PR with no checks reports `pending`, and never turns green.** The combined
+  status API returns `state: "pending"` with `total_count: 0` when *nothing has
+  reported*, which is indistinguishable at a glance from "checks still running".
+  Any instruction to "merge when it is green" therefore never terminates; gate on
+  `mergeable_state` instead, and check `total_count` before believing `pending`.
+  This is §4's blocker wearing a different hat: a check that never reports reads
+  as a check still coming.
 
