+**Confirmed again 2026-08-23, with the reason.** `add_repo` refuses with
+*"repository name `.github-private` begins with '.', so its clone directory would
+be a hidden path"*. The seed-and-`add_repo` fallback above therefore does not
+work for this repo either — and the consequence is worse than "no attach": the
+session git proxy serves anonymous reads of **public** repositories only, so a
+*private* dot-named repo has no read fallback at all. `.github` is public and
+clones read-only fine, which is enough to port from but not to land in.
+`list_repos` still reports `.github-private` with `can_push: true`. The
+permission exists; the transport does not. **The web selector is the only
+route.**
